{"id":"h278","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-chemistry","question":"The X-band (9.5 GHz) EPR spectrum of a matrix isolated Na atom reveals four hyperfine lines with resonant field positions of 3074 G, 3174 G, 3274 G and 3374 G. Calculate the g value of the atom.\nIs the correct answer \"g = 2.020\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct answer is NO; g is about 2.105, not 2.020.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The resonance condition hν = gβB gives g = hν/(βB).","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The four lines are equally spaced by 100 G, the hyperfine splitting for Na with I = 3/2.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The centre of the hyperfine pattern, 3224 G, is the correct resonance field for extracting g.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Using the centre field, the formula gives g of about 2.105.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Matrix isolation can shift g from the free-atom value of about 2.0023, so a value near 2 is plausible.","confidence":0.6,"lean":1,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The 3374 G line alone gives g of about 2.012, close to 2.020, so 2.02 is not absurd.","confidence":0.4,"lean":1,"theta":0.6283,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Obtaining g = 2.020 requires a field of about 3360 G, which is not the centre of the pattern.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The value 2.020 does not follow from the stated data.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.6